}

You can only cast to objcnames.protocols.ForwardDeclaredProtocolProtocol from the corresponding real class. Otherwise, you'll get an error.","title":"Interoperability with Swift/Objective-C","source":"https://kotlinlang.org/docs/native-objc-interop.html","sections":["Interoperability with Swift/Objective-C > Mappings > Forward declarations"],"line_start":510,"line_end":517,"score":0.6000484228134155,"release_version":null,"availability":"unknown"},{"anchor":"native-swift-export.md","start":922,"end":1654,"split_code":false,"platforms":["native"],"id":"a66ada3185027af85bebfed4da0c60d0f6b42c97bd064805e3d008826f7d178c","document_id":"native-swift-export","strategy":"semantic","text":"Enhanced nullability for primitives . Unlike Objective-C interop, which required boxing types like Int? into wrapper classes like KotlinInt to preserve nullability, Swift export converts nullability information directly.

